    {
      "node_id": "kg_doc_4",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "Stephen John Coogan (born 14 October 1965) is an English actor, stand-up comedian, impressionist, screenwriter, and producer. He began his career in the 1980s, working as a voice artist on the satirical puppet show \"Spitting Image\" and providing voiceovers for television advertisements. In the early 1990s, he began creating original comic characters, leading him to win the Perrier Award at the Edinburgh Festival Fringe. In 1999, he co-founded the production company Baby Cow Productions.",
      "depth": 0,
      "parent_id": null,
      "value": 0.999999998128988,
      "temperature": 0.999999998128988,
